    "title": "Beech Grove Schools Warn Of Deep Cuts As New Referendum Takes Center Stage - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Sarah Thompson ,\n1 days ago Beech Grove City Schools is rolling out a summer series of public meetings starting tonight, as district leaders make their case for a proposed 2026 operating referendum that they say keeps buses running, buildings maintained and safety staff on the job. The first session is set for today 6 p.m. at Beech Grove High School. District officials stress that the proposal is meant to replace the operating referendum voters approved in 2020 and to protect day-to-day services rather than pay for new construction. Read full article\n1",
